  "goodToKnow": "Zocken originally meant gambling, from Rotwelsch (old thieves' slang) and probably related to Yiddish. Today it mostly means playing video games: Wir zocken heute Abend. Der Zocker is a gambler or a gamer, and verzocken means to gamble away. It's informal, so you won't write it in a formal text. The neutral word for gaming is Computerspiele spielen."
